[5] SENSITIVITY -- month-varying flux weight (the choice flagged in [3])
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  NH month-varying: half-amp 1.1682 K (fixed-weight FLUX 3.0813) -> -62.1 %
  SH month-varying: half-amp 0.3267 K (fixed-weight FLUX 2.0104) -> -83.7 %

  ⛔ THIS IS NOT A BRACKET ENDPOINT AND IS DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED BELOW.
     Two reasons, either sufficient. (1) THE BOX MODEL CANNOT REPRESENT IT:
     the parameter multiplies ONE prescribed cycle on ONE box, so its honest
     analogue is sum_i wbar_i T'_i(t) with a FIXED wbar. A time-varying w_i(t)
     adds a rectification term the box has no way to carry, so this number
     answers a question the parameter does not ask. (2) THE WEIGHT COVARIES
     WITH WHAT IT WEIGHTS: |flux| carries dpCO2, and dpCO2's seasonality is
     itself partly driven by the SST cycle being measured. That is circular,
     and it is the likelier explanation of a -84 % collapse than any physics.
     ⇒ Reported because it is large and someone will otherwise compute it and
     believe it. NOT interpretable as either a bracket end or a clean
     rectification estimate without a k field.

